From 19e9b81fee563c27c98a40186f312e1e28704ca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edmund-landgraf <114525624+edmund-landgraf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:50:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Require a user JWT or API key on every function except
 public content reads

connect() now rejects calls with no token, the anon key, or an unverifiable JWT unless the endpoint opts in with allowAnonymous (content lookups, search-data, get-content-versions, get-content-source-stats). API keys work only on character endpoints and are scoped to characters granted to that client and owned by the key's user; find-character list calls are narrowed to that grant set.
